    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Majapahit was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#hindu-buddhist">Hindu-Buddhist</a> kingdom in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#java">Java</a> that dominated the archipelago's sea lanes in the 14th century.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rice">Rice</a> from the Brantas valley and control of the spice trade funded fleets, temples and a network of tribute-paying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#vassal">vassals</a>.</li><li>Civil war, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#malacca">Malacca</a>'s rise and Muslim coastal sultanates such as Demak eroded it; its court culture lived on in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#bali">Bali</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Majapahit's founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#raden-wijaya">Raden Wijaya</a> used a Mongol army sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> to defeat his rival, then turned on the invaders and drove them from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#java">Java</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

